\ Regression test: a quotation embedded in a container literal resolves its own module-private word
\ when the extracted quotation is `call`ed from a context where that module's frame is not live.
\
\ The companion's `handlers` returns an `H{ }` table whose value is `[ tag ]`, where `tag` is
\ module-private. This file extracts that quotation and calls it at its own top level. Without
\ container stamping the quotation carries no defining module, so `tag` fails to resolve.

use "testing" ;
use { handlers: } "./module_deps_container_holder.1z" ;

"container-embedded quotation resolution" test-section

handlers probe: @get call
"LIB-TAG" "container-embedded quotation resolves its module-private word from a neutral context" assert=
